  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1128 PM CDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nAn upper level ridge will build over the plains by mid to late week,\nin advance of an upper level trough along the west coast. The \nridge will bring above normal temperatures to West Central Texas \nduring the day, with highs mainly in the low to mid 80s Wednesday \nthrough Friday, while overnight lows will be mainly in the 50s.\n\nThe upper ridge will shift eastward Friday night into the \nweekend, as the upper storm system to the west pushes east across\nthe southern Rockies. Still some model differences regarding the \nevolution of this system this weekend into the following week, but\nNBM low to medium (20%-40%) rain chances seem reasonable for now.\nIn addition to the rain chances, cooler temperatures will return,\nwith highs in the 70s from Sunday through the following Tuesday.",
